G1 — DESIGN CALL AND HUNKS
--------------------------
  Decided shape: KEEP the relationship (matches #16's modelling intent and pins
  `field_path` ordering at the mapping) and eager-load it with
  `selectinload(Asset.assertions)` at the `_asset_to_dict`-feeding query sites where the
  eager load survives to serialization. `_asset_to_dict` now iterates `asset.assertions`.
  A K-asset serialization therefore costs ONE assertion SELECT (constant in K).
  `selectinload` NOT added at PATCH (:399) / MERGE (:483): their services commit and
  `db.refresh()` the instance, which discards a preloaded collection; measured PATCH = 3
  with the option vs 2 without (pre-slice also 2), so omitting it preserves the count.
  This is a finding against the packet's flat "selectinload at every site" hint (F3).
  Cascade: relationship needs `cascade="all, delete-orphan"` (schema FK is
  `ondelete="CASCADE"`); without it the ORM nulled `assertion.asset_id` on
  `session.delete(asset)` and broke test_search (F4, fixed in-slice).

  Hunks (CO-100: verified no secret-like token within the app diff):
    backend/app/models/asset.py     + relationship assertions (order_by, cascade)
    backend/app/models/assertion.py + relationship asset (back_populates)
    backend/app/api/v1/assets.py    selectinload import; 3 query sites get the option;
                                    `_asset_to_dict` iterates asset.assertions; stale
                                    `Assertion` import dropped; 2 explanatory comments
    backend/tests/test_sg136_assertion_batch.py  + fixture baseline (from G0)

